===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|slang|pejorative|lang=en}} An obese or otherwise swollen ankle that blends into the calf without clear demarcation.
#* '''2001''', ''[[w:Shallow Hal|Shallow Hal]]'':
#*: Hey, all l’m saying is she’s got '''cankles''', for God’s sake. ''What?'' '''Cankles'''! She’s got no ankles. It’s like the calf merged with the foot, cut out the middleman. 
#* {{quote-book|year=2004|passage=The “'''cankle'''” (or the appearance of not having an ankle, but the calf of the leg just connecting to the foot) is a look that many women have and most could live without.|author=Jeff Smith|title=Posing for Portrait Photography: A Head-to-Toe Guide}}
#* {{quote-book|year=2005|passage=They’d pass me magazines and ask how my '''cankle''' recovery was progressing.  They’re ankles, not '''cankles'''.  I don’t have '''cankles'''!|author=Franz Wisner|title=Honeymoon with my Brother}}
#* '''2007''', ''Family Guy'', season 5, "Bill And Peter's Bogus Journey":
#*: Now that's a cankle! Where does the calf fat end and the ankle fat begin? Who knows, that's the fun! 
#* '''2008''', 13 September, ''Saturday Night Live'':
#*: Amy Poeler as Hillary Clinton: Stop saying I have '''cankles'''!

